3. PERMITTED ACTIVITIES

Users may:

a. Download the Software from an official source
   authorized by the Licensor.

b. Install and use the Software on personally owned
   computers or other computers they are authorized
   to use.

c. Examine the Software's source code for learning,
   research, troubleshooting, or personal development.

d. Modify the Software for their own private use.

e. Compile and execute privately modified versions
   of the Software.

f. Create reasonable backup copies solely for
   their own use.

g. Report bugs, submit feedback, and suggest
   improvements.

h. Share links to official distribution locations
   without redistributing the Software itself.

4. REDISTRIBUTION PROHIBITED

Users may not redistribute the Software or any
Modified Version without prior written permission
from the Licensor.

This restriction applies regardless of whether
distribution is commercial or noncommercial.

Prohibited redistribution includes, but is not
limited to:

a. Uploading copies to websites, repositories,
   file-sharing services, or other distribution
   platforms.

b. Sharing original or modified executable files
   with other individuals.

c. Publishing or sharing modified source code,
   patches containing protected portions of
   the Software, or derivative versions.

d. Mirroring or rehosting official releases.

e. Including the Software in another software
   package, collection, installer, or product.

f. Distributing copies through physical media,
   private file transfers, or public downloads.

Users may direct others to the official download
location instead.

5. COMMERCIAL EXPLOITATION PROHIBITED

Users may not, without prior written permission:

a. Sell the Software or any Modified Version.

b. Charge fees for providing copies of the Software.

c. Rent, lease, sublicense, or license the Software
